rg33 automatic placement of trailing constants and variables

// Regression for the automatically emitted constants and variables blocks.
// It guards against three defects, all silent:
//   - the block stamped with whatever bank happens to be current when the
//     program ends, not the bank it belongs to, so it can land in, and
//     overwrite, another bank
//   - variables allocated before constants by the parser but emitted after
//     them by a code generator, so the variables are written past the
//     constants instead of where their symbols point
//   - a code generator advancing the bank's cur_pc, so whichever one runs
//     second reports or emits the block at the wrong address
//
// Both banks leave constants and variables dangling, and the program ends in
// bank 0, so bank 1's trailing block is the one most likely to be misplaced.
// Compared against the stored .ref, which pins bank and address for every word.

100/
       lac [foo:1             // a bank 0 constant holding a bank 1 address
       dac v1
       lac [0d1234
       dac v2
       hlt
bar,   0                      // referenced from bank 1

var v1
var v2

bank 1
200/
foo,   0                      // referenced from bank 0
       lac [bar:0             // a bank 1 constant holding a bank 0 address
       dac w1
       hlt

var w1

bank 0
start 100
